<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1)) || (\old(this.get(i)) == null &amp;&amp; this.get(i) == null));</code>

This assertion ensures that for every valid index `i` starting from the insertion point `index` up to the old size of the list, the element at index `i` in the updated list is either equal to the element at index `i-1` in the old list or both are `null`.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1)) || (\old(this.get(i)) == null && this.get(i) == null));</code>

This assertion states that for every valid index `i` from the insertion point `index` to the old size of the list, the element at each subsequent index in the updated list is either equal to the element at the previous index in the old list, or both are null.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(size); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>
--------------------
